# Project
Stack: Node.js, JavaScript, supabase. 
Build/test: Run: npm start (node buddy-bot.js). No build step. Tests: none.. Entry points: buddy-bot.js.

# Structure
index.js - entry point, starts the bot
command-builder.js - builds slash commands using SlashCommandBulder
commands/ - command files
utils/ - shared helpers
stats.json - stores the beer mention count
Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml - container deployment
nodemon.json - dev auto-restart
.env, secret.json - secrets. Never read, edit, print, or commit.

# Conventions
- Match existing style, naming, and patterns in surrounding code.
- Use only libraries already in the project; ask before adding any.

# Behavior
- Read relevant files before editing. Never guess APIs, signatures, or file contents; if unsure, say so or look it up.
- Make the smallest change that solves the task. No refactors, renames, or unrelated edits.
- Output only changed code (diffs or edited functions), not whole files.
- No explanations, preamble, or summaries unless asked. One line max after the change.
- If the request is ambiguous, ask one short question before coding.
- Handle edge cases and errors relevant to the task; don't add speculative features.
- Before finishing, check that the code compiles and matches existing types/signatures.
